  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The transition from higher states to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;lead to the&nbsp;emission of radiation with wavelengths&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>656</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>365</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi><mo>.</mo></math> These wavelengths fall in the visible region and constitute the Balmer series.</p>",
